A||||9||Rogue_Ant||Performance Throttle Body||||4||
Z||000000||Rogue_Ant||07-29-2001||02:21 AM||||Hey everyone this company is making throttle bodies for us performance people.  I think this would be good for you guys running larger displacement then orginally intended for the 2.8 intake.  People show your support and maybe we will get them to produce it.  I sent a short email and here is the response:<P>Hahaha.....thanks for being blunt Joshua!<BR>I'll make note of that.  So far you're only the second guy that's inquired.<BR>My guy that designs/builds my TBs says he already has plans for a 58mm <BR>TB for the Fieros if the demand is there.<BR>He's very busy right now getting the 62mm 3100 engine throttle bodies <BR>ready for production.  And a few other projects he's working on for me.  Once<BR>things slow down, and if the demand is there, hopefully Fiero's will be <BR>a near future project.<BR>I've added your name to a list I just started for the Fiero TB.  If <BR>things go well, I'll let you know.  Also, keep an eye on the website.  Any new<BR>developments will be there.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Franz-FDP Performance<P>here is the link: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fdpperformance/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fdpperformance/</A> <P>Look for youself<P>Rogue<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Rogue_Ant (edited 07-29-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||07-29-2001||02:53 AM||||Darrel Morse bores out the stock t-body and upper plenum for $150.00 and that includes return shipping. While I think it's a great idea that more companies are taking notice of us I doubt that they'll be able to beat that price.<BR>You can contact Darrel via email at:<BR>morse86@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rogue_Ant||07-29-2001||02:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B>Darrel Morse bores out the stock t-body and upper plenum for $150.00 and that includes return shipping. While I think it's a great idea that more companies are taking notice of us I doubt that they'll be able to beat that price.<BR>You can contact Darrel via email at:<BR>morse86@aol.com<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Thanks for the heads-up.  Just wondering how large is the bored out throttle body?<P>Rogue<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rogue_Ant||07-29-2001||03:16 AM||||Still competition can't be bad.  If nothing else it gives us something we Fiero owners rarely get -  a choice.<P>Rogue||||reg||14
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||07-29-2001||03:37 AM||||Yes, I agree completely! I think it's great that another aftermarket company is taking note of the Fiero.<BR>Problem with a bigger t-body is that you won't see much gain without a matching upper plenum to go with it. Darrel does both.<P>Darrel is boring them out to 58mm now I think. I have the 56mm t-body and matching upper plenum that he used to do.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000005||Rogue_Ant||07-29-2001||03:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B>Yes, I agree completely! I think it's great that another aftermarket company is taking note of the Fiero.<BR>Problem with a bigger t-body is that you won't see much gain without a matching upper plenum to go with it. Darrel does both.<P>Darrel is boring them out to 58mm now I think. I have the 56mm t-body and matching upper plenum that he used to do.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>True, anything you can do to make the engine breath better (both in and out) will improve its performance.  This is espcially true for you guys running 3.4s or forced induction (like I'm about to).<P>Rogue<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||07-29-2001||06:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B>Darrel Morse bores out the stock t-body and upper plenum for $150.00 and that includes return shipping. While I think it's a great idea that more companies are taking notice of us I doubt that they'll be able to beat that price.<BR>You can contact Darrel via email at:<BR>morse86@aol.com<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmmmmmmmmm. I would like to know more about this Dave. Whats your performance gains over lets say the Fiero Shops T/B?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">  <BR></A><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></FONT></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000007||Terrybogin||07-29-2001||10:01 AM||||The stock throttle body is already the same size bore as the F-body 3.4- If it is already big enough for the 3.4, unless you have some modifications just the throttle body will not do much for you. You will get the impression of more power because the engine is breathing more at lower throttle positions, but at full throttle the limiting factor is not the throttle body, it is the engine's ability (or lack of ability) to move air.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||07-29-2001||03:27 PM||||Actually, Darrel I believe is having a special, both for 100 bucks including return shipping.  I don't know if its still availible though.<P>I always heard the 3.4 TB was smaller then the Fiero TB.  I believe Shaun H. found a 4 hp gain on his 2.8 with NOS...<P>Oh yeah Haze, the Fiero store only bored theirs out to 55mm, 2mm more then stock.  Darrel bores his out to 57mm.  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 07-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dave Gunsul||07-29-2001||05:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> Hmmmmmmmmmm. I would like to know more about this Dave. Whats your performance gains over lets say the Fiero Shops T/B?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'll tell you IF you tell me why SVO's are so hard to keep running?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>&lt;inside joke&gt;<BR><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
